body:
@phene Ouch!

@mschulkind and @phene, I am very willing to break backward compatibility. @mschulkind nailed it when he said "I fear there is code out there relying on this". Given that someone will complain, which users do we not want to complain? What are valid uses of `#reprocess!` that we want to make sure continue to work, and which should we toss? And of those valid uses, is there a better solution than `#reprocess!`?

(While we do use Paperclip, we do not use all the features of it in every app. Not sure when I last used `#reprocess!`.)
